Third-party recipe content

Original starter recipes
app/lib/demo-recipes.ts contains original RAG Chef starter recipes distributed
under this repository's MIT license. They are separate from both the synthetic
test fixtures and the third-party evaluation corpus described below. Loading
them is an explicit setup action; it does not copy the user's kitchen.

Wikibooks Cookbook
The Wikibooks entries in tools/recipes/fixtures/relevance-catalog.json and the
source excerpts in tools/recipes/core-dinners.v1.json,
tools/recipes/core-dinners.v2.json,
tools/recipes/extra-dinners.v1.json,
tools/recipes/extra-dinners-2.v1.json,
tools/recipes/extra-dinners-3.v1.json and
tools/recipes/verified-times.v1.json are attributed to Wikibooks
contributors under CC BY-SA 4.0. Each record retains its source URL and attribution;
the source page history identifies contributors. Extraction normalizes formatting.
The timing annotations retain source statements and reviewed revision links;
numeric values normalize number wording and use the upper bound of a source range.
The v2 dinner review refreshes original source notes and records why incomplete
or inconsistent source time labels remain unknown; ingredients, directions and
source servings are retained without changes.
The additional-dinner review records source-specific assessments; the source
recipes are collected separately from the linked Wikibooks pages.
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights

The reviewed boiling and simmering definitions in app/lib/chef-context.ts are
paraphrases of the following Wikibooks Cookbook pages, by Wikibooks contributors,
under CC BY-SA 4.0. They are displayed separately from recipe facts, with source
and license links. Their page histories identify contributors.
https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Boiling
https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Simmering

TheMealDB
Six entries in tools/recipes/fixtures/relevance-catalog.json originate from
TheMealDB's official API. Each retains its source attribution and links.
They are not represented as CC BY-SA content. TheMealDB's terms govern API content
use, including keeping copyright/trademark notices; any third-party material has
its own permission requirements. The app's adapter uses the documented development
API and does not grant a license to the upstream collection or artwork.
https://www.themealdb.com/api.php
https://www.themealdb.com/terms_of_use.php

The frozen corpus is an evaluation fixture, not an application seed or a copy of
the user's kitchen. Dependency licenses and notices remain with their packages.
The MIT license in LICENSE applies to original app code, not the third-party
recipe corpus, source excerpts or dependencies described above.
